cite70†Tagline L119:     * cite71†The arXiv Voice L120:   * [Input]\nL121: \nL122: cite72†Labs L123: \nL124: Labs\nL125:     * cite73†arXivLabs: Showcase L126:   * [Input]\nL127: \nL128: cite74†Policies L129: Policies\nL130:     * cite75†Code of conduct L131:     * cite76†Privacy policy L132:     * cite77†Identity, affiliation, and registration L133:     * cite78†Submittal agreement L134:     * cite54†Authority Records L135:     * cite18†Submission Overview L136:     * cite25†Availability of submissions L137:     * cite79†Content Moderation L138:     * cite29†Licenses L139:     * cite40†Withdraw / Retract a Submission L140:     * cite26†Category cross listing L141:     * cite37†Translations L142:     * cite80†Non-English submissions L143:     * cite39†Why Submit TeX? L144:     * cite36†Proxy / Third Party Submission L145:     * cite81†Copyright Infringement L146:   * cite82†Categories†arxiv.org L147:   * cite83†arXiv Usage Stats L148: Table of contents\nL149:   * cite0†Open Archives Initiative (OAI) L150:     * cite84†Notes for harvesters L151:       * cite85†Base URL L152:       * cite86†Identify response and policies L153:       * cite87†Item = Article L154:       * cite88†Metadata formats L155:       * cite89†Datestamps L156:       * cite90†Sets L157:       * cite91†Update schedule L158:     * cite92†Chronology L159:       * cite93†March 2025 L160:         * cite94†Major differences: L161:         * cite95†Minor differences: L162:       * cite96†12 April 2007 L163:       * cite97†1 April 2007 L164:       * cite98†29 December 2006 L165:       * cite99†2 July 2003 L166:       * cite100†20 June 2001 L167:       * cite101†21 January 2001 L168:       * cite102†15 February 2000 L169:       * cite103†27 January 2000 L170:       * cite104†21-22 October 1999 L171: # Open Archives Initiative (OAI)\nL172: \nL173: arXiv supports and participates in the cite105†Open Archives Initiative†www.openarchives.org (OAI). arXiv is a registered OAI-PMH cite106†data-provider†www.openarchives.org and provides metadata for all submissions which is updated each night shortly after new submissions are announced. Metadata for arXiv articles may be reused in non-commercial and commercial systems.\nL174: \nL175: Please review the cite107†Terms of Use for arXiv APIs before using the arXiv OAI-PMH interface.\nL176: ## Notes for harvesters\nL177: \nL178: ### Base URL\nL179: \nL180: arXiv supports cite108†OAI_PMH v2.0†www.openarchives.org at the baseURL cite109†https://oaipmh.arxiv.org/oai?verb=Identify†oaipmh.arxiv.org .\nL181: \nL182: ### Identify response and policies\nL183: \nL184: Policy links and various other details are included in the cite109†Identify†oaipmh.arxiv.org response.\nL185: ### Item = Article\nL186: \nL187: Each article in arXiv is modeled as an Item in the OAI-PMH interface. Only the most recent version of each article is exposed via this interface (some metadata formats include the version history).\nL188: ### Metadata formats\nL189: \nL190: Metadata for each item (article) is available in several formats, all formats are supported for all articles. The available formats include:\nL191: \nL192:   * `oai_dc` - Simple Dublin Core. See cite110†example in `oai_dc` format†oaipmh.arxiv.org .\nL193: \nL194:   * `arXiv` - arXiv specific metadata format for the latest version of a paper. Includes author names separated out, category and license information. See cite111†example in `arXiv` format†oaipmh.arxiv.org .\nL195:   * `arXivRaw` - arXiv specific metadata format which is very close the internal format stored at arXiv. Includes history for previous versions of the paper. See cite112†example in `arXivRaw` format†oaipmh.arxiv.org .\nL196: \nL197: You may request a list of all the metadata formats supported with the cite113†ListMetadataFormats†oaipmh.arxiv.org verb.\nL198: ### Datestamps\nL199: Every OAI-PMH metadata record has a cite114†`datestamp`†www.openarchives.org associated with it, which is the last modification time of that record. To view dates for previous versions of a paper use the arXivRaw metadat format. Because arXiv has updated metadata records in bulk on several occasions, the OAI-PMH `datestamp` values do not correspond with the original submission or replacement times for older articles, and may not for newer articles because of administrative and bibliographic updates.\nL200: The earliest datestamp is given then the `<earliestDatestamp>` element of the cite115†Identify†oaipmh.arxiv.org response.\nL201: > Please Note: The OAI-PMH interface does not support selective harvesting based on submission date. The datestamps are designed to support incremental harvesting of updates on an ongoing basis. It is not possible to selectively harvest articles such as articles submitted in February 2001. With the exception of selective subject area harvesting cite90†(see description of Sets below) the interface is designed to support copying and synchronization of a complete set of arXiv metadata.\nL202: To harvest metadata for all articles:\nL203: >\nL204: >   * Make requests without a datestamp range (recommended)\nL205: >   * Make requests from the `<earliestDatestamp>` through to the present\nL206: >\nL207: > (Beware: due to bulk updates, some dates contain large numbers of updates).\nL208: Once an initial harvest has been completed, the copy may be maintained by making incremental harvesting requests with the `from` date set to the date of last harvest (`from` is best taken from the last server response; don't set the `until` date).\nL209: ### Sets\nL210: Specific categories, archives, and groups are available for selective harvesting. Archives are subsets of groups and categories are subsets of archives. This means that a single catgory can be selected for harvesting with the set `cs:cs:AI`, a whole archive with the set `physics:hep-th`, or all physics archives with the set `physics`. Alternatively all of arXiv can be harvested by not specifying a `setSpec`. You may request a list of all the sets supported with the cite116†ListSets†oaipmh.arxiv.org verb.\nL211: ### Update schedule\nL212: \nL213: New papers are accepted daily and metadata is made available via the OAI-PMH interface once they are announced, typically around 10:30pm ET Sunday through Thursday. Occasional small changes to paper data may happen intermittently throughout the day.\nL214: \nL215: ## Chronology\nL216: \nL217: ### March 2025\nL218: \nL219: A total rewrite of the system.\nL220: #### Major differences:\nL221:   * Base URL updated from `http://export.arxiv.org/oai2` to `https://oaipmh.arxiv.org/oai`\nL222:   * Earliest start date: from 2007-05-23 to 2005-09-16\nL223:     * All papers modified before 2005 are now included, but all share the same earliest modified date\nL224:   * Change to historical modified dates for a small number of papers\nL225:   * Set expansion\nL226:     * The set structure has become more precise to include group, archive, and category specification\nL227:     * All previous set memberships are still valid, but sets can be requested and will be identified more specifically now\nL228:     * Follows structure group:archive:CATEGORY Example math:math:NA or physics:hep-lat\nL229:     * Full list can be found at cite116†ListSets†oaipmh.arxiv.org L230: #### Minor differences:\nL231: \nL232:   * Papers in alias categories included in both sets\nL233:   * Resumption token no longer counts total items in list, or cursor, and expires daily\nL234:   * Increased limit on results\nL235:   * mSource flags appear more consistently in arXivRaw format\nL236:   * Change in order of record items to match schema\nL237: ### 12 April 2007\nL238: \nL239: The arXiv OAI baseURL changed to `http://export.arxiv.org/oai2` from `http://arxiv.org/oai2`. The old URL will issue a redirect for some time but please update your harvester to use the new baseURL.\nL240: \nL241: ### 1 April 2007\nL242: \nL243: Support for the long-deprecated cite108†OAI_PMH v1.1†www.openarchives.org at baseURL `http://arXiv.org/oai1` has been discontinued. Please use our v2.0 interface instead.\nL244: ### 29 December 2006\nL245: \nL246: arXiv Dienst interface disabled. The Dienst protocol was replaced by the OAI-PMH and arXiv's interface hasn't been used regularly by any service for a few years and not at all in the last few months.\nL247: \nL248: ### 2 July 2003\nL249: \nL250: cite108†Open Archives Initiative Protocol for Metadata Harvester v2.0†www.openarchives.org is released. arXiv supports both OAI-PMH v1.1 and v2.0; v1.1 is deprecated.\nL251: ### 20 June 2001\nL252: \nL253: Minor update of the OAI protocol to follow changes in the XML Schema specification, arXiv updated to support cite117†OAI-PMH v1.1†www.openarchives.org .\nL254: \nL255: ### 21 January 2001\nL256: \nL257: cite118†Open Archives Initiative Protocol for Metadata Harvester v1.0†www.openarchives.org released, the Santa Fe Convention is discontinued. See cite105†OAI website†www.openarchives.org for details of the latest protocol.\nL258: ### 15 February 2000\nL259: \nL260: cite119†The Santa Fe Convention†www.openarchives.org officially released, arXiv is compliant.\nL261: \nL262: ### 27 January 2000\nL263: \nL264: arXiv Dienst implementation for Santa Fe Convention compliance announced to participants in the Open Archives initiative.\nL265: ### 21-22 October 1999\nL266: \nL267: cite119†The Santa Fe Convention†www.openarchives.org was the result of a meeting of the Open Archives initiative held in Santa Fe, New Mexico, USA.\nL268: \nL269: We gratefully acknowledge support from our major funders, cite120†member institutions , , and all contributors.\nL270: \nL271: cite121†About · cite122†Help · cite123†Contact · cite124†Subscribe · cite29†Copyright · cite76†Privacy · cite125†Accessibility · cite126†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L272: \nL273: Major funding support from\n"
